W3.2d.7.7 prerequisite — L6 Flow and Text alignment
Oracle authorization: da61acfa-164a-426a-8e6b-bc65450b0aa4.
Reference handoff: 1911a490-83e7-4ca9-bb3c-b05afd8285f6.

Mechanism:
crates/bbt-ui/src/components.rs — retained Flow packs children in source order,
  with wrap, main justification, cross alignment and independent row/column
  gaps, then delegates each row to the existing Stack allocator. No grid.
  Text.align defaults to Start and offsets each wrapped line independently;
  collapsible trailing whitespace does not enter the alignment width.
crates/bbt-ui/tests/flow.rs — four focused regressions: wrapping/baselines/gaps,
  nowrap/space-between/exact fit, multiline alignment, fitting Stack equivalence.
crates/bboxybook/src/components.rs — public web Stack options map to Flow;
  Text alignment maps to the retained Text. No browser child positions consumed.
crates/bboxybook/capture-exercises.mjs — acceptance witnesses only: Flow must
  exercise row counts [2,2,1], and the centred caption must span multiple lines.
  Missing witnesses fail capture; they never become native layout input.

Reference correction:
5579278 rendered a deep-linked case at full width; the first 40-case comparison
  passed but did not exercise wrapping. That run is retained as flow/first and
  is not acceptance evidence for wrapping. Wren corrected the host width in
  41f17803c2542bfeab9d453e2db00f7fa77157ed. All eight new Flow cases now show
  [2,2,1] rows, and all eight text-align cases show a wrapped centred caption.
  Existing box/text/stack hosts retain their original widths.

